  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A **Web API** is an interface that allows different software systems to communicate over HTTP. **REST** (Representational State Transfer) is an architectural style for designing APIs."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "REST Principles"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Stateless**: Each request contains all necessary information",
          "**Resource-based**: URLs represent resources (nouns, not verbs)",
          "**HTTP methods**: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE for CRUD operations",
          "**JSON**: Standard data format for requests and responses"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "HTTP Methods"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": [
          "Method",
          "Purpose",
          "Example"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "GET",
            "Read data",
            "/api/users"
          ],
          [
            "POST",
            "Create data",
            "/api/users"
          ],
          [
            "PUT",
            "Update data",
            "/api/users/1"
          ],
          [
            "DELETE",
            "Delete data",
            "/api/users/1"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "info",
        "title": "Status Codes",
        "text": "Use appropriate HTTP status codes: 200 (OK), 201 (Created), 400 (Bad Request), 404 (Not Found), 500 (Server Error)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "Web APIs enable system communication",
          "REST is an architectural style",
          "HTTP methods map to CRUD",
          "Use appropriate status codes"
        ],
        "takeaway": "REST APIs are the standard for web services."
      }
    }
  ]
}
